Z||000000||FieroFanaticus2||03-31-2001||06:25 PM||||I have an 88 Coupe That likes to Idle funny.<BR>It'll start up fine and Idle at about .8, then drop to about .4 or so, almost dying, then spring back up to normal idle.<BR>It'll do this when I start it up, then at stop lights/signs.  Sometimes it'll actually kill on me.  Also, sometimes when I accellerate in first gear it'll chug a little bit (RPM's drop) unless I give 'er some extra gas.  Some mechanic told me it's the IAC valve, but that he didn't want to change it unless he had to, this is also the guy who wanted to charge me nearly $300 to replace a single caliper.  I'm thinking the idle problem could be either the IAC Valve or the PCV.  Maybe ( I am no mechanic ) even the fuel filter or pump?  If anybody has any ideas PLEASE PLEASE PLEASE let me know!  Thanks --- FieroFanaticus  (michael)||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroFanaticus2||03-31-2001||10:00 PM||||Anybody?||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||03-31-2001||10:18 PM||||start looking for vacuum leaks. check both ends othe the PCV line. clamp PCV elbows. replace MAT sensor. MAT is in the intake manifold to right of the TBI.<P>other wise read in my cave and use the forum search system. cave link at bottom of page.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 03-31-2001).]||||reg||1
